      ],
      "extract_7_codes": [
        "1",
        "10",
        "12",
        "21",
        "22",
        "32",
        "34",
        "36"
      ],
      "note": "Both extracts carry the same eight EMPSTAT codes. {10,12} is what the pre-event builder KEPT, not what the data holds. A builder that assumes only {10,12} arrive would silently drop the 41.5% of extract-7 rows that are unemployed (21,22), not in the labour force (32,34,36) or armed forces (1).",
      "zero_padding": "Armed Forces arrives as '1', not '01'. String compares against '01' match nothing."
    },
    "month_coverage": {
      "expected_if_contiguous": 57,
      "missing": [
        "2025-10"
      ],
      "months_present": 56,
      "note": "2025-10 is absent from IPUMS entirely -- no cps2025_10 sample and no 'October 2025' description among the full 670. The panel has a real one-month hole. A builder that assumes 56 contiguous months, or that computes month-over-month differences without checking the gap, will be wrong across the 2025-09/2025-11 boundary."
    },
    "uhrsworkt_beyond_997_999": {
      "answer": "YES, and it was already true of extract 6",
      "extract_6_n_distinct": 107,
      "extract_7_max_non_sentinel": 172,
      "extract_7_n_distinct": 123,
      "note": "UHRSWORKT carries actual hours across 0-172 alongside 997 (hours vary) and 999 (NIU). In extract 7: 999 appears 66,106 times and 997 10,023 times, leaving 166,345 rows with a real hours value. Treating 997/999 as hours would inflate mean hours by orders of magnitude; treating every value as a sentinel would empty the column."
    }
  },
